  {
    "id": "2d82db05923f8cac2e552db4",
    "path": "arrow_json::reader::ReaderBuilder::with_ignore_type_conflicts",
    "name": "with_ignore_type_conflicts",
    "owner": "arrow_json::reader::ReaderBuilder",
    "crate": "arrow-json",
    "version": "59.3.0",
    "kind": "function",
    "signature": "fn with_ignore_type_conflicts(self, ignore_type_conflicts: bool) -> Self",
    "docs": "Sets whether the decoder should produce NULL instead of returning an error if it encounters\nvalue that can not be parsed into the specified column type.\n\nFor example, if the type is declared to be a nullable array of `DataType::Int32` but the\nreader encounters a string value `\"foo\"` and the value `ignore_type_conflicts` is:\n\n* `false` (the default): The reader will return an error.\n\n* `true`: The reader will fill in NULL value for that array element.\n\nNOTE: An inferred NULL due to a type conflict will still produce parsing errors for\nnon-nullable fields, the same as any other NULL or missing value.",
    "span": {
